        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The American public is capable of understanding complex constitutional arguments and making informed judgments.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "An impeachment trial serves as a moral and civic referendum on the health of American democracy.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "A 'definitive' national statement on authoritarianism requires high-stakes political engagement.",
        "confidence": 0.84
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the current political climate reflects deeper existential challenges to liberal democracy.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience values narrative coherence between past actions and present outcomes in political leadership.",
        "confidence": 0.82
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker sees the impeachment process as a vehicle for shaping long-term democratic norms.",
        "confidence": 0.81
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92776,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92776.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "You know, is this America, you know, I was hoping back at the impeachment trial, that that would be an easy question for people to answer, that the senators who had just lived through the violence of the insurrection, who had just lived through an attempted political coup, would say, no, we can demonstrate the legislative self-respect the bicameral self-respect, the constitutional self-respect to say, no, we're not going to accept these kinds of violent assaults on the sovereignty of the people and the autonomy of Congress under the Constitution. I mean, the GOP punted, everybody punted, and then it came to the people. And in the election, You know, I don't know that the people punted necessarily, but the half plus sum that won basically said, for whatever reason, we understand that there was this assault on the Constitution and on the democracy, but it's not as important to us as some other things.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Senators experienced the violence of the January 6th insurrection and the attempted political coup firsthand.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The Republican Party avoided taking a principled stand during the impeachment process.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The impeachment trial was expected to be a clear moment for Americans to affirm their commitment to democratic principles.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The senators failed to uphold legislative, bicameral, and constitutional self-respect during the impeachment trial.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The responsibility to respond to the constitutional crisis ultimately fell to the electorate.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "In the subsequent election, voters did not prioritize the defense of constitutional democracy over other concerns.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Legislators have a moral obligation to defend the constitution against threats, especially after experiencing direct violence.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Public officials should act based on principle rather than political expediency when facing existential threats to democracy.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "There exists a shared understanding among citizens about what constitutes legitimate democratic governance.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The electorate has sufficient awareness and capacity to recognize constitutional violations.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "A majority vote reflecting indifference toward constitutional integrity signals a failure of civic duty.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
