    "turn_text": "Victor Orban's government, a white Christian nationalist administration where the president sacks large parts of the government, replaces them, with party and personal loyalists and flunkies and sycophants. And then one person basically runs the whole country like an autocrat in corrupt association with oligarchs, Putin style, who were able to make out like bandits with no legal scrutiny or legal regulatory supervision, right? And then they will govern on the basis of scapegoating and bashing minorities and so on. That's scary. It's scary. But look, I mean, I'm talking about this in a conversational tone of voice because I think we have to. This is for real. And there are lots of people who are scared. There are obviously millions of undocumented immigrants in the country and other kinds of immigrants who are scared about what's going on. There are lots of civil rights, civil liberties groups who are scared, and there are various people who've been identified as political enemies of Donald Trump who are just trying to prepare reasonably as they should for what might come. But we can't let the fear paralyze us. That's the key thing. We've got to act with a lot of courage. And we did it the first time around. And we've seen a lot of people acting with courage. And one person's courage emboldens other people. And we've got to hang tough for the Constitution and for democracy.",
